  "body": "What: add the document-level post option `Explain` (default off, per-setup override) to `PostOptions`; `posting::options_value` publishes `postOptions.Explain = true` only when on (off stays byte-identical, like smoothing #616). Add the PRELUDE helper `explain(words)` (crates/post/src/post/js.rs) with the shared original wording table, manifest keys `explains = \"paren\" | \"semi\"` and `commentMax`, and the engine guards: comment text cleaned to printable ASCII without delimiters, ACTIVE-keyword lead guard (MSG/DEBUG/PRINT/LOG/PY...) for every dialect, truncation to `commentMax` that never touches the executable words. A post without `explains` is refused by name when Explain is on, before any hook runs.\nWhy: design in the research comment on #1358.\nEvidence: assets/posts/AGENTS.md (programUnits refusal pattern, #902), tormach.cps ACTIVE guard (#594).\nDone means: with Explain on, a test script using `explain()` gets comments in both syntaxes; a post lacking `explains` is refused by name; with Explain off every existing golden is byte-identical; a test strips comments from the Explain-on output and asserts it equals the Explain-off program; undo of the option works.\n\nPart of #1358\n",
